  icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: bbec7a84e96ca95458eba143068d1dd0, type: 3}
  title: Timeflow Presets
  sections:
  - heading: Presets Overview
    text: 'Timeflow offers a custom preset system with the ability to create presets
      for individual components (Component Presets) and complex object presets (Advanced
      Presets). '
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Component Presets
    text: 'This type of preset is used to save and apply settings for specific components.
      These store a list of property values, which can target all or only select
      properties. Component Presets in some cases can also store channel and animation
      data.  '
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Advanced Presets
    text: 'These presets are based on prefabs and therefore can store complete objects
      and hierarchies with full animation. Advanced Presets can be instantiated as
      new objects, or stamped onto existing objects either replacing or merging components.
      This can include any type of component, including animations.


      Open
      the Advanced Presets Window to manage and work with these presets.'
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: How to Apply Presets
    text: 'Click the presets icon in the Timeflow view. For objects this invokes
      the Advanced Presets menu. For channels, a drop down menu is displayed for
      Component Presets. You can also apply and save presets from the component menu
      (3 dots) in the inspector. This is available for all component types, not just
      Timeflow. '
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Creating Presets
    text: "From the menus mentions above, select Save Preset to create your own.
      This opens the preset creation window where you can select which properties
      to save. Only the selected properties get saved and applied, making it possible
      to create a variety of presets that can target different parameters. \n\nPreset
      assets may be organized however you wish in the project. "
    linkText: Presets Documentation
    url: https://axongenesis.gitbook.io/timeflow/user-guide/menus-and-shortcuts/presets
  loadedLayout: 0
  isEditing: 1
